   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing by hand; I assigned each @/@@ from the wedge and hash geometry, so a stereo error is possible.\n\n**Aglycone.** It is a spirostanol steroid with the usual four fused rings (A\u2013D) plus the spiroketal. Substituents:\n- a 2-OH on ring A and an O-glycoside at C3;\n- methyl groups at C10 and C13;\n- a 15-OH next to the furan oxygen on C16;\n- a C20 methyl;\n- a spiro tetrahydropyran carrying the C25 methyl.\n\n**Sugar chain at C3-O.**\n1. A hexopyranose (first sugar) is attached through its anomeric carbon to the C3 oxygen. Its C4 oxygen links to the next sugar.\n2. A second hexopyranose is attached at that C4 oxygen. Its C3 oxygen carries a pentopyranose, and its C2 oxygen carries a third hexopyranose.\n3. The pentopyranose is a xylose-type sugar with no CH2OH.\n4. The third hexopyranose carries a fourth hexopyranose on its C3 oxygen.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H]1CC[C@@]2(OC1)O[C@H]3[C@@H](O)[C@H]4[C@@H]5CC[C@H]6C[C@@H](O[C@@H]7O[C@H](CO)[C@H](O[C@@H]8O[C@H](CO)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O[C@@H]%11OC[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]%11O)[C@@H]8O[C@@H]9O[C@H](CO)[C@H](O)[C@H](O[C@@H]%10O[C@H](CO)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]%10O)[C@H]9O)[C@H](O)[C@H]7O)[C@H](O)C[C@]6(C)[C@H]5CC[C@]4(C)[C@H]3[C@@H]2C"
